## What I found

`/luxon/src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js` had a hard-coded `isValid` getter:

```js
  /** @override **/
  get isValid() {
    return true;
  }
```

The constructor stores `this.fixed = offset` with no validation, and `FixedOffsetZone.instance(offset)` passes any value through (`offset === 0 ? utcInstance : new FixedOffsetZone(offset)`). So `FixedOffsetZone.instance("bogus")` reported `isValid === true`, and since `DateTime`'s constructor / `setZone` / `fromObject` / `fromJSDate` all gate on `!zone.isValid` (→ `unsupportedZone(zone)` → `Invalid("unsupported zone", ...)`), a DateTime in that zone stayed valid. `IANAZone` does the analogous thing via a `valid` field computed in its constructor; `InvalidZone` returns `false`. `isNumber` is `typeof o === "number"` in `src/impl/util.js`.

